{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/helperbuilds"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"How one helper source tree becomes two binaries, and how each feature finds out whether it can run.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacKit"}],"title":"The App Store and Direct builds"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuilds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Headwire Helper ships in two builds from the same code:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The App Store build"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is sandboxed and has everything that needs no private API, input included. It is the default: a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift build"},{"type":"text","text":" makes it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Direct build"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is signed with Developer ID, notarized and unsandboxed. It adds only the code compiled under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HEADWIRE_PRIVATE_API"},{"type":"text","text":": the virtual display that extends the Mac onto the device or gives a Mac with no display one, Apple’s Sidecar started from the menu, and answering the Mac’s side of Bluetooth pairing without a system dialog. Each of these is checked at run time and turns off rather than crashes when macOS has changed it."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper input is compiled under a second switch, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HEADWIRE_HELPER_INPUT"},{"type":"text","text":", which is on by default in both builds and is turned off only should App Review refuse event posting. A build without it keeps streaming and shows input as unavailable."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This documentation is generated from the App Store build, so the Direct build’s private-API types do not appear in it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Which build is running","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Which-build-is-running"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/current"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the two compile-time switches and reports the build’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/Distribution-swift.enum"},{"type":"text","text":" and whether helper input is compiled in. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/launchLine(version:dryRun:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the first line the helper logs at launch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Whether a feature runs","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Whether-a-feature-runs"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperFeatures\/resolve(_:grants:build:)"},{"type":"text","text":" combines three inputs into one "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState"},{"type":"text","text":" for each feature:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The menu’s switch for it, in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperToggles","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Every switch starts off: the helper is optional, and streaming, input and extending the Mac begin only when the person turns them on."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What macOS has granted, in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/PermissionGrants"},{"type":"text","text":". A switch that is on without its permission is "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needs(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Onboarding"},{"type":"text","text":" walks the person through that one permission."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What the build contains. A feature the build lacks is "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/unavailable(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" with an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability\/menuText"},{"type":"text","text":" is shown on the greyed-out control."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The extended display also needs streaming, so with its switch on and streaming not running it is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needsStreaming","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The features go to the device as the helper’s capabilities, so the device greys out the same controls with the same reasons."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://HeadwireMacKit/documentation/HeadwireMacKit/Un